  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Cody Bellinger turned a tied game into a rout with one swing, and the Yankees took what they needed.",
    "what_this_means": "Max Fried was immaculate through six innings. One run on three hits, six strikeouts. And the lineup finally converged behind him. It was not close late. Bellinger went 2-for-5 with four RBI, his two-run homer in the sixth the moment the game broke open into a six-run inning. Luis Garc\u00eda Jr. added a solo shot and three more hits. The offense produced 14 hits and 10 strikeouts; they chose to score, not struggle. Will Warren and David Bednar finished clean in relief. This was an offensive breakout wearing the shape of a complete game. And it arrived exactly when the division pressure needed something to give. They were 4.5 back. One win does not close that gap. But a blowout at home against Boston, behind elite pitching and broad hitting, looks like the kind of night that sticks.",
    "what_to_watch": "Tampa Bay arrives tonight with Drew Rasmussen on the mound. A 2.67 ERA that has looked untouchable in October baseball. And Gerrit Cole gets the ball back. The bullpen just proved it can hold late. Now the starter has to give them innings.",
